From 935843a61cea787aede0b3eb3602b45afaf2657c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:38:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 052/149] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: Mark the video codec
 dma-coherent

The video codec's non-secure context bank is IO-coherent: the vendor
device tree marks it so (dma-coherent-hint-cached on the venus_ns
context bank), and so does mainline for the newer SoCs' iris nodes.

Without it the decoded frames are mapped uncached, and every reader of
a frame (a player copying it out, a GL upload) reads uncached memory:
on a Surface Duo 2, mpv with the v4l2m2m-copy decoder in a GTK player
took 92 % of a CPU core for 1080p30 H.264, 43 % with the codec marked
coherent. H.264, HEVC (1080p and 2160p) and VP9 decode bit-exactly to
the software decoders with it, and the HFI queues work as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
index 7d4c13f7aef5..9144bc2243e0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
@@ -3002,6 +3002,7 @@ &config_noc SLAVE_VENUS_CFG QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>,
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&iris_opp_table>;
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2100 0x400>;
+			dma-coherent;
 			memory-region = <&pil_video_mem>;
 
 			status = "disabled";
